    {
      "id": "31skm8b",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Radius and General Facts about the Earth"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Earth is structurally divided into three concentric layers: Crust, Mantle, and Core.",
        "The Crust consists of Continental Crust (SIAL - Silica and Aluminium) and Oceanic Crust (SIMA - Silica and Magnesium).",
        "The Mantle extends to a depth of 2,900 km and contains the Asthenosphere, the primary source of magma.",
        "The Core is composed mainly of Nickel and Iron (NIFE), featuring a liquid Outer Core and a solid Inner Core.",
        "Seismic boundary zones called discontinuities (e.g., Moho, Gutenberg) mark abrupt changes in density and wave velocity."
      ],
      "id": "fjyjdip"
    },
